WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.593 --> 00:00:15.558
Tommy Stubbins had big dreams.

2
00:00:16.078 --> 00:00:20.039
He dreamt of one day visiting faraway lands and seeing the world.

3
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.202
But for now, his life was in Puddleby, where nothing much exciting happened.

4
00:00:25.222 --> 00:00:28.343
"Tommy, take these to Colonel Bellowes.

5
00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:29.563
And be quick about it!"

6
00:00:30.043 --> 00:00:31.004
his father urged.

7
00:00:33.388 --> 00:00:35.910
Tommy's father was the shoemaker in Puddleby.

8
00:00:36.231 --> 00:00:38.673
He wanted Tommy to follow in his footsteps.

9
00:00:39.593 --> 00:00:42.316
But Tommy was not interested in fixing shoes.

10
00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.880
People like Colonel Bellowes upset him.

11
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.583
"Your shoes, sir," Tommy said, smiling.

12
00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:53.125
The colonel rudely grabbed the shoes.

13
00:00:54.066 --> 00:00:55.627
Tommy wanted to kick the door.

14
00:00:57.328 --> 00:01:01.292
Fortunately, before Tommy could do that, a sound caught his attention.

15
00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:03.777
He found a wounded squirrel.

16
00:01:04.537 --> 00:01:09.139
Tommy was not fond of mean men like the Colonel, but he did love animals.

17
00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:12.641
"You poor thing," he said gently.

18
00:01:13.181 --> 00:01:15.842
He could not see what was causing the squirrel pain.

19
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:20.164
Tommy decided to take the squirrel home.

20
00:01:20.944 --> 00:01:24.706
Along the way, he ran into Matthew, a friendly old man he knew.

21
00:01:24.726 --> 00:01:27.887
"What have you got there, Tommy?"

22
00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:29.248
Matthew pointed.

23
00:01:29.928 --> 00:01:33.250
"A squirrel, but I don't know what's wrong with it," he answered.

24
00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.032
"You need to see Dr.

25
00:01:37.132 --> 00:01:39.053
Dolittle," Matthew advised.

26
00:01:39.073 --> 00:01:40.194
"Who is he?

27
00:01:40.554 --> 00:01:41.255
Is he a vet?"

28
00:01:41.715 --> 00:01:42.335
asked Tommy.

29
00:01:42.956 --> 00:01:44.857
Matthew looked shocked.

30
00:01:44.877 --> 00:01:47.038
"He's better than a vet!"

31
00:01:47.418 --> 00:01:48.158
he exclaimed.

32
00:01:48.179 --> 00:01:54.282
"One time, my duck Lulu was sick, so I took her to see the doctor."

33
00:01:54.302 --> 00:01:56.463
"What was the matter with her?"

34
00:01:56.903 --> 00:01:57.584
Tommy asked.

35
00:01:58.216 --> 00:01:59.016
"Be patient.

36
00:01:59.337 --> 00:02:00.697
I'm getting to that part."

37
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:02.558
Matthew cleared his throat.

38
00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:11.722
Dolittle used to be a human doctor, but he realized he wanted to help animals."

39
00:02:11.742 --> 00:02:13.143
"Like me!

40
00:02:13.523 --> 00:02:15.104
I like helping animals, too."

41
00:02:15.124 --> 00:02:18.685
"Do you want to hear this story or not?"

42
00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.046
Matthew sighed loudly.

43
00:02:21.066 --> 00:02:24.488
"Oops! Sorry," Tommy apologized.

44
00:02:25.252 --> 00:02:26.734
"Not only does Dr.

45
00:02:26.814 --> 00:02:35.421
Dolittle help animals," Matthew said, then lowered his voice mysteriously, "but he can speak their language, too!"

46
00:02:35.441 --> 00:02:37.983
"What?!" Tommy shouted.

47
00:02:40.425 --> 00:02:42.447
Matthew told Tommy the whole story.

48
00:02:43.268 --> 00:02:45.690
Dr. Dolittle had examined Matthew's duck.

49
00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:50.474
"You have a very bad throat," the doctor had told Lulu.

50
00:02:50.974 --> 00:02:52.756
"You mustn't quack so loudly."

51
00:02:53.564 --> 00:02:54.825
"But I can't help it!

52
00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:57.487
Those cows keep coming to my pond!"

53
00:02:58.088 --> 00:02:58.908
quacked Lulu.

54
00:02:58.929 --> 00:03:03.392
"Dr. Dolittle and the duck talked to each other?"

55
00:03:03.913 --> 00:03:05.294
Tommy could not believe it.

56
00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:07.095
Matthew nodded.

57
00:03:07.115 --> 00:03:10.117
"They made strange clucking sounds."

58
00:03:10.138 --> 00:03:11.999
"Could you understand it?"

59
00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:12.980
asked Tommy.

60
00:03:14.221 --> 00:03:15.342
Matthew shook his head.

61
00:03:15.362 --> 00:03:19.005
"No, I don't have the gift.

62
00:03:19.425 --> 00:03:22.928
Dr. Dolittle had to explain to me what they talked about."

63
00:03:23.932 --> 00:03:27.895
Then, Matthew said, the doctor wrote something on a slip of paper.

64
00:03:27.915 --> 00:03:32.599
"Lulu, I'm going to give this to Matthew," the doctor said.

65
00:03:32.619 --> 00:03:34.401
"What is it?"

66
00:03:34.941 --> 00:03:35.762
quacked Lulu.

67
00:03:36.522 --> 00:03:42.627
"Every day you must drink juice made of barley, grass, onions, and carrots," Dr.

68
00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:43.728
Dolittle explained.

69
00:03:44.529 --> 00:03:45.750
"Yuck! Quack!"

70
00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:47.151
shrieked Lulu.

71
00:03:49.252 --> 00:03:50.854
"Lulu!" Dr.

72
00:03:50.894 --> 00:03:52.375
Dolittle said sternly.

73
00:03:53.748 --> 00:03:55.850
"Uh, doctor, is she all right?"

74
00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.571
Matthew was worried.

75
00:03:57.591 --> 00:03:58.912
"Yes, Matthew.

76
00:03:59.192 --> 00:04:03.595
Just make sure she drinks this juice every day," said the doctor.

77
00:04:03.615 --> 00:04:05.776
"Did the juice work?"

78
00:04:06.137 --> 00:04:07.197
Tommy wanted to know.

79
00:04:07.217 --> 00:04:12.101
"Lulu was back to normal in a few days," Matthew replied.

80
00:04:12.761 --> 00:04:14.402
Matthew began walking again.

81
00:04:14.983 --> 00:04:16.323
Tommy walked beside him.

82
00:04:16.343 --> 00:04:18.865
"I wonder if he can help this squirrel?"

83
00:04:19.285 --> 00:04:20.466
Tommy asked hopefully.

84
00:04:20.486 --> 00:04:23.813
"John Dolittle can do it," said Matthew.

85
00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:26.815
"But I'm afraid he's not here right now."

86
00:04:28.396 --> 00:04:29.057
"Where is he?"

87
00:04:29.497 --> 00:04:30.177
Tommy asked.

88
00:04:30.197 --> 00:04:32.879
"Well, he's on a voyage, of course.

89
00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.441
He loves to travel the world!"

90
00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:36.882
Matthew exclaimed.

91
00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:39.244
Tommy's eyes got bright.

92
00:04:39.264 --> 00:04:42.547
"I wonder if one day I can travel with him?"

93
00:04:42.947 --> 00:04:43.768
he said aloud.

94
00:04:44.888 --> 00:04:47.651
Unknown to Tommy, his wish would soon come true.
